HIV/Qaeda: China has reported a 14% increase
"China has reported a 14% jump in the number of new cases of citizens living with HIV and AIDS.
More than 820,000 people in the country have been affected, health officials say.
About 40,000 new cases were recorded alone in the second quarter of 2018.
The vast majority of new cases have been transmitted through sexual intercourse, which is a change in relation to the previous situation.
In the past, HIV has spread rapidly across some parts of China as a result of blood transfusions of the virus.
However, the number of people receiving HIV has been reduced almost to zero, Chinese health officials said at a news conference in Yunnan province.
However, year after year, the number of people in China living with HIV and AIDS has risen by about 100,000.
Transmission of HIV through sexual intercourse is a burning problem in China's LGBT community.
Homosexuality has been no longer regarded illegal in China since 1997, but say discrimination against an LGBT person has been spreading.
Studies have estimated that due to conservative understandings in the country, 70–90% of men who have a sex relationship with men eventually engage with women.
The transmission of the virus often arises due to inadequate sexual protection in such relationships.
In 2003, the Chinese government pledged universal access for HIV drugs as part of a plan to address this problem.
